invariant: INV-11
file: srv_kex.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: the server puts the x25519 shared secret ahead of the ML-KEM one in
  the input keying material, which is the order the group's name
  suggests and the reverse of the one RFC 10024 fixes. Both halves are
  still secret, so nothing on the server's side notices; the client
  derives other handshake keys and the first sealed record fails.
  test_flight_hybrid_secret derives the client's keys from the
  ServerHello's own bytes and compares them with the server's.

--- old
        memcpy(ikm, h->mlkem_ss, MLKEM_SS_LEN);
        ecdhe = ikm + MLKEM_SS_LEN;
--- new
        memcpy(ikm + X25519_LEN, h->mlkem_ss, MLKEM_SS_LEN);
        ecdhe = ikm;
